# PX4 parameters laid over the benchmark's set when a profile has a `gps` block (the runners
# do this themselves): the bridge's scripted GPS is the receiver, EKF2 fuses it beside the
# vision stream (docs/field-faults.md, "GPS on"; sim2real/estimate_bridge/gps.py).
#
# MAV_USEHILGPS 1: PX4's mavlink receiver turns the bridge's HIL_GPS into sensor_gps.
# SIM_GPS_USED 0: Gazebo's own navsat receiver reports no fix, so PX4's GPS selection takes
#   the bridge's (a receiver with no fix is never selected, and never blended).
# EKF2_GPS_CTRL 7: fuse GPS horizontal position, height and 3D velocity (PX4's default).
# SYS_HAS_GPS 1: the preflight GPS checks run, as on a GPS-equipped drone.
1	1	MAV_USEHILGPS	1	6
1	1	SIM_GPS_USED	0	6
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	7	6
1	1	SYS_HAS_GPS	1	6
# EKF2_HGT_REF 0: the barometer is the height reference. PX4 v1.17 numbers this 0 = barometer,
#   1 = GPS, 2 = range sensor, 3 = vision. The benchmark set says 0 too since 2026-11-02 (it
#   said 1 before, which with GPS on would be GPS height); kept here so this file stands alone.
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	0	6
